# Force LF line endings on everything that gets copied to and run on the
# KINDLE, regardless of the developer machine's git settings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: this repo is developed on Windows, where git's
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this machine is set
# to) rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for the
# Windows-side backend, but the Kindle runs busybox on Linux, where a
# shell script with CRLF line endings fails immediately and confusingly:
#
#     /bin/sh: ./run.sh: /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
#     ./run.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#
# The working tree happened to be correct because these files were
# authored with LF and never re-checked-out -- but a fresh `git clone` on
# a Windows machine would have produced broken copies of every on-device
# script, with a failure mode that looks nothing like a line-ending
# problem to whoever hits it.

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.lua  text eol=lf

# Windows-side scripts: keep CRLF. .bat in particular can misbehave with
# LF-only endings under cmd.exe.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
